           (and (= :variable (nth row 1))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1309:                (:vm/store-get :vm/store-put)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1341:                 {:role :variable, :name definition-operator}))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1345:                 {:role :variable, :name definition-operator})))))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1368:                              (if (and slots (= (count slots) (dec (count (subvec row 1)))))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1376:                                        (range 1 (inc (count slots))) slots (rest (subvec row 1)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1404:                                   body (subvec row 1)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1411:                                       body (subvec row 1)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1422:                                        body (subvec row 1)]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1462:   `(subvec row 1)` through `jing/materialize!`, which derives exactly the\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1473:    (jing/materialize! handle (subvec row 1)))\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1535:                 body (subvec row 1)\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1636:   Clause order is load-bearing: `[(< ?n ?m)]` guards the `subvec` range,\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1646:     [(subvec ?path 0 ?n) ?lam-path]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1652:  \"§7.7 free-name extraction as a function: every `:variable` name free at\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1667:                               [$ast ?v :variable ?name]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1702:   profile effects (§7.7.2). A `:variable`'s name obligation is\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1716:           :vm/store-get #{},\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1720:           :literal #{}, :variable #{}, :lambda #{}, :application #{}, :if #{}},\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1730:                :store-get #{},\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1762:                                 [$ast _ :vm/store-get ?key]\nsrc/cljc/yin/vm.cljc:1765:                                      [$ast ?op :variable ?name]\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"The re-keying appears to close the frozen-export path: the readers, top-level definitions, and init replacements all use `js.rt/*`, which export selection excludes. I also confirmed a correction to the cost estimate: `data/subvec` copies each tail here, so a full lookup can allocate O(n²) elements. I’m assessing that as retention/performance debt rather than a provenance failure."}}
